ccess","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Rule 22e-4 treatment of a qualifying \"In-Kind ETF\"**\n\nA qualifying In-Kind ETF meets redemptions in kind, using cash only de minimis, and keeps written policies on how it determines that status.\n\n**Still required:**\n- **Written liquidity risk management program:** adopt it, assess and manage liquidity risk, and review it at least annually.\n- **15% illiquid-investment limit:** identify illiquid assets to monitor the cap.\n- **Breach response:** if illiquid assets exceed 15%, report to the board and file Form N-RN.\n- **Board oversight:** the board approves the program administrator and receives an annual written report on the program's adequacy and effectiveness.\n- **Recordkeeping and related N-PORT reporting.**\n\n**Relief:**\n- **No four-bucket classification:** the fund need not classify holdings as highly liquid, moderately liquid, less liquid or illiquid. It only identifies illiquid assets.\n- **No highly liquid investment minimum (HLIM):** this also removes the related shortfall policies and board reporting.","ttft_ms":2923,"type":"result","duration_ms":2937,"uuid":"ca1d655a-8d3a-4bbe-8d59-feb502c214a9","ttft_stream_ms":496,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":496,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
